In the figure, point G is the midpoint of BC, point H is on AF, and point P moves along the edge of the figure at a speed of 2 cm per second. The path of movement is: G→C→D→E→F→H. The area of triangle ABP, denoted as y (cm²), is a function of the time t (s) as shown in the second figure. Given that AB = 6 cm, how many of the following six conclusions are correct? 
1. The length of BC in the first figure is 8 cm; 
2. The point M in the second figure indicates that the value of y at the 4th second is 24 cm²; 
3. The length of CD in the first figure is 4 cm; 
4. The length of DE in the first figure is 3 cm; 
5. The point Q in the second figure indicates that the value of y at the 8th second is 33; 
6. The point N in the second figure indicates that the value of y at the 12th second is 18 cm².
A. 3
B. 4
C. 5
D. 6

