As shown in the figure, a taxi departs from point A and travels in a direction of 60° north of east to reach point B. After that, it travels in a direction of 50° south of east to reach point C, which is directly east of point A. Which of the following statements are correct? ( ) 
① B is 50° north of west from C; 
② The angle between roads AB and BC is 110°; 
③ A is 30° north of west from B; 
④ The angle between roads AC and BC is 50°.
A. ①②
B. ③④
C. ①③
D. ②④
